If I can set it up at the very beginning, gosh, my carer will talk about anything with me, I've just increased the likelihood they're going to come to me when those kinds of events occur. So let me switch gears for a minute and ask, how do factors like race, socioeconomic, or disability intersect with trauma, both exposure and recovery? Great question, because I think we do need to go there. Because if we don't talk about it, again, we're not going to be able to understand or address it. We know COVID showed us in neon lights that more. marginalized populations, people of color, people with lower socioeconomic status, were less likely to receive services, have access to services, and they were more likely to have worse outcome from the pandemic.
如果我能在最开始就建立好这一点：“天哪，我的照顾者会和我谈论任何事”，我就刚刚提高了他们在这些事件发生时来找我的可能性。所以让我转换一下话题，问一个问题：诸如种族、社会经济地位或残疾等因素如何与创伤（包括暴露和恢复）交织在一起？这是一个很好的问题，因为我认为我们确实需要探讨这个话题。因为如果我们不谈论它，我们就无法理解或解决它。我们知道新冠疫情（COVID）以霓虹灯般醒目的方式向我们展示了：更多边缘化群体、有色人种、社会经济地位较低的人，获得服务的可能性更低，获得服务的渠道更少，而且他们更有可能从大流行中承受更糟糕的结果。

