consultation and services, we're meeting them where they are. But yeah, we do see that individuals, that racial differences, SES differences, have different outcomes. It's often because they don't have the same access to services. We also see that there is still, I mean, I would love to say, gosh, we've been doing psychology for a long time. There's no stigma around mental health. That would be a lie. There's still stigma.
